course: dictionary
lesson: 10496
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Tut can be a sound, an action, or a name. Read the words around it to find out which one it is.
explain: «She tutted at the noisy boys.» Here tutted is an action. Someone made a small clicking sound with their tongue to show they were annoyed. Ask yourself: is the word doing something, naming something, or making a sound?
explain: «King Tut» is different. Here Tut is a short name for Tutankhamun, a young pharaoh of ancient Egypt. Capital letters and a name before or after the word are clues that it is a name.
fact: A tut is a small clicking sound made with the tongue.
fact: People tut to show they disapprove or are annoyed, often without saying a word.
fact: «Tut-tut» is a sound you can write down, and it often shows you think someone has done something wrong.
fact: «King Tut» is short for Tutankhamun, a young pharaoh of ancient Egypt.
fact: The tomb of Tutankhamun was found in 1922.
exercise: «She tutted at the noisy boys.» What does tutted mean here? | To make a clicking sound to show you are annoyed | * To sing a happy tune | To fall over and hurt yourself | To run very fast
exercise: «King Tut» is a short name for which famous pharaoh? | Tuba | Tutu | Tutor | * Tutankhamun
exercise: Dad gave a loud tut when he saw the mess. What is a tut? | A type of Egyptian tomb | A bright light | A long walk | * A small clicking sound made with the tongue
test: «Tut-tut» on its own shows what? | * You disapprove or are annoyed | You have won a prize | You are going to sleep | You are very hungry
test: In the words «King Tut», Tut is short for what? | A tutu dancer | A tuba player | A tutor who teaches | * Tutankhamun, a young pharaoh of Egypt
exam: Which sentence uses tut as a verb, an action word? | Tut-tut, said the bus driver. | Tutankhamun was a pharaoh of Egypt. | The tut from the bus driver was loud and clear. | * The queue was long, and Gran tutted at the delay.
